# Generated by cryptogen (NET-1) — throwaway dev-grade MSP/TLS material, never
# the production identity path (that's NET-2, Fabric CA). Regenerable from
# network/crypto-config/crypto-config.yaml; must never be committed.
# No trailing slash on the extra lines below: relocating these outside the
# repo via a symlink was attempted 2026-08-09 but reverted — Docker Desktop's
# bind-mount source resolution fails with "mkdir ...: file exists" when a
# symlink sits on a mounted subpath (confirmed against this compose file's
# deeply-nested per-node mounts). Currently real directories again, but a
# trailing-slash pattern only matches real directories, not a symlink to one
# — kept both forms so re-attempting a different relocation strategy later
# doesn't silently lose this protection.
network/crypto-config/ordererOrganizations
network/crypto-config/ordererOrganizations/
network/crypto-config/peerOrganizations
network/crypto-config/peerOrganizations/

# Generated by configtxgen (NET-1) — regenerable from network/configtx/configtx.yaml.
# Same symlink-relocation note as above applies here.
network/channel-artifacts
network/channel-artifacts/*.block
network/channel-artifacts/*.block.*

# Generated by fabric-ca-client enroll/register (NET-2) — throwaway dev identities,
# regenerable from network/fabric-ca/*-config.yaml + enrollment-runbook.md.
network/fabric-ca/enrollments/
network/fabric-ca/.tls-certs/

# Generated by go mod vendor / peer lifecycle chaincode package (CC-5) —
# regenerable; the tar.gz is a build artifact, vendor/ is derived from go.sum.
chaincode/employeeprofilerecord/vendor/
chaincode/employeeprofilerecord/employeeprofilerecord.tar.gz
chaincode/employeeprofilerecord/ccaas-package/code.tar.gz

# Go tool binaries (CC-5/NET-3/NET-6) — build with `go build`, don't commit.
tools/*/netjoin
tools/*/raftfaulttest
tools/*/ccdeploy
